# Bricks Design System — all values must be token-mapped

**Source of truth:** Bricks DS **v1.2.0** in `design-system/tokens/` (+ archive zip).  
**Figma:** use the enabled **Bricks Design System** library only — bind existing library variables / text styles. **Never create** new variables or text styles.

Every visual value on UI (code or Figma) must attach to a mapped Bricks token. Not just color — **radius, spacing, font, type size/weight/line-height/letter-spacing, and text styles** too.

## Token map (look here first)

| Concern | Token file | CSS bridge | Figma library collection |
|---|---|---|---|
| Color primitives | `color_primitives.Value.tokens.json` | `--ds-color-*` | `color_primitives` |
| Color semantic | `color_tokens.Value.tokens.json` | `--ds-*` semantic | `color_tokens` |
| Spacing / gap / padding | `spacing.Value.tokens.json` | `--ds-space-*` | `spacing` |
| Corner radius (rounded) | `radius.Value.tokens.json` | `--ds-radius-*` | `radius` |
| Type primitives | `typography.value.tokens.json` | `--ds-font-*` etc. | `typography` |
| Text styles | `text.styles.tokens.json` | existing text style names | library text styles |

Font family from DS: **Google Sans Flex** (`typography.font_family.primary`). Weights: Regular / Medium / SemiBold / Bold only as tokenized.

## Hard rules

- **Bind or reference the token** — do not hardcode `12px`, `8px`, `border-radius: 16px`, `font-size: 15px`, Inter/system fonts, raw hex, etc. when a Bricks token exists.
- In **CSS/React**: only `--ds-*` (or established DS class/tokens already wired from this pack).
- In **Figma / figma-cli**: `importVariableByKeyAsync` / bind from **Bricks Design System** library; apply existing text styles — never `variables.create`, never `createTextStyle`, never raw fills/sizes “because it’s a quick test.”
- Prefer **semantic** tokens when they exist; otherwise primitives from the same pack.
- If no token fits → **stop and ask**. Do not invent a one-off value or extend the DS unless the user explicitly requests it.

## Before setting any property

1. Identify the concern (color / radius / space / type / text style).
2. Look up the matching token in `design-system/tokens/` or the Bricks library.
3. Use / bind that mapped value only.
